*---------------------------------------------------------------
* readdir.equ -- the RD_* record offsets, split out of
* readdir.s so they can be `put` BEFORE the code that uses them.
*
* Real Merlin-8 refuses a unit that references an `equ` in an
* immediate operand before the `equ` is assembled ("Illegal
* forward reference", reported against the definition line);
* merlin32 iterates to a fixed point and accepts it silently.
* du.s, find.s and ls.s all index this record with `ldy #RD_*`
* hundreds of lines before they `put` readdir.s, so the offsets
* have to arrive first. The RECORD LAYOUT itself is documented
* in readdir.s's own header, which is still where it belongs --
* only the five equates move.
*
* An `equ` emits nothing, so this split is byte-neutral by
* construction; the objects were compared to prove it.
*---------------------------------------------------------------

RD_LEN      equ   0         ;1  name length
RD_NAME     equ   1         ;16 name + NUL, case-decoded
RD_FTYPE    equ   17        ;1  file_type
RD_STYPE    equ   18        ;1  storage_type
RD_EOF      equ   20        ;3  EOF, little-endian, RAW
RD_MDATE    equ   23        ;2  mod_date, little-endian, RAW
RD_MTIME    equ   25        ;2  mod_time, little-endian, RAW
RD_BLOCKS   equ   27        ;2  blocks_used, appended in old pad
RD_SIZE     equ   32

* -- docs/DEVFS.md, 2026-09-30: RD_STYPE_BLK/RD_STYPE_CHR moved
* -- here for the SAME reason as the five offsets above --
* -- lsprint.s/lstop.s (ls.s's own front/print halves) `put`
* -- BEFORE readdir.s in ls.s's expansion order, and need them
* -- too. Still readdir.s's layout to own; only the two equates
* -- move.
RD_STYPE_CHR equ  $0A       ;a character device (ttys, null)
RD_STYPE_BLK equ  $0B       ;a block device (/dev/sNdM)
